###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_139356
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_139356> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33697> ;
                                              <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "An immature or incompletely processed mRNA molecule that needs to be processed before it becomes a fully functional mature mRNA. Pre-mRNA is synthesized from a DNA template in the cell nucleus by transcription and lacks structures that the mRNA requires. First all introns have to be removed from the transcribed RNA through a process known as splicing. Before the RNA is ready for export, a Poly(A)tail is added to the 3' end of the RNA and a 5' cap is added to the 5' end." ;
                                              <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> "chebi_ontology" ;
                                              <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> "CHEBI:139356" ;
                                              <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#inSubset> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/3_STAR> ;
                                              rdfs:label "precursor messenger RNA" .


