###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17761
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17761> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_26739> ,
                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_37622> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Ceramides (<em>N</em>-acyl-sphingoid bases) are a major subclass of sphingoid base derivatives with an amide-linked fatty acid. The fatty acids are typically saturated or monounsaturated with chain lengths from 14 to 26 carbon atoms; the presence of a hydroxyl group on carbon 2 is fairly common. Ceramides are generally precursors of more complex sphingolipids. In the illustrated generalised structure, R<small><sup>1</small></sup> = OH, OX (where X = acyl, glycosyl, phosphate, phosphonate, etc.), or H." ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasAlternativeId> "CHEBI:12487" ,
                                                                                                             "CHEBI:13954" ,
                                                                                                             "CHEBI:23074" ,
                                                                                                             "CHEBI:7242" ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> "chebi_ontology" ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> "CHEBI:17761" ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#inSubset> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/3_STAR> ;
                                             rdfs:label "ceramide" .


