###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35366
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35366> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_18059> ,
                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_25384> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Any aliphatic monocarboxylic acid derived from or contained in esterified form in an animal or vegetable fat, oil or wax. Natural fatty acids commonly have a chain of 4 to 28 carbons (usually unbranched and even-numbered), which may be saturated or unsaturated. By extension, the term is sometimes used to embrace all acyclic aliphatic carboxylic acids." ;
