                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_52557> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Esters of phorbol, originally found in croton oil (from <em>Croton tiglium</em>, of the family Euphorbiaceae). A number of phorbol esters possess activity as tumour promoters and activate the mechanisms associated with cell growth. Some of these are used in experiments as activators of protein kinase C." ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> "chebi_ontology" ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> "CHEBI:37532" ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#inSubset> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/3_STAR> ;
                                             rdfs:label "phorbol ester" .


