###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_4056
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_4056> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_35137> ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A cytochrome is a hemoprotein whose characteristic mode of action involves transfer of reducing equivalents associated with a reversible change in oxidation state of the prosthetic group. Formally, this redox change involves a single-electron, reversible equilibrium between the Fe(II) and Fe(III) states of the central iron atom." ;
                                            <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> "chebi_ontology" ;
