                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_52684> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A butanediol that is butane in which one hydrogen of each of the methyl groups is substituted by a hydroxy group. A colourless, water-miscible, viscous liquid at room temperature (m.p. 16°C) with a high boiling point (230°C), it is mainly used for the production of other organic chemicals, particularly the solvent oxolane (also known as tetrahydrofuran or THF)." ;
