###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_75632
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_75632> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_26195> ,
                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_26267> ,
                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_50128> ,
                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_72010> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A proanthocyanidin consisting of two molecules of (−)-epicatechin joined by a bond between positions 4 and 8' in a β-configuration. Procyanidin B2 can be found in <em>Cinchona pubescens</em> (Chinchona, in the rind, bark and cortex), in <em>Cinnamomum verum</em> (Ceylon cinnamon, in the rind, bark and cortex), in <em>Crataegus monogyna</em> (Common hawthorn, in the flower and blossom), in <em>Uncaria guianensis</em> (Cat's claw, in the root), in <em>Vitis vinifera</em> (Common grape vine, in the leaf), in <em>Litchi chinensis</em> (litchi, in the pericarp), in the apple, in <em>Ecdysanthera utilis</em> and in red wine." ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> "chebi_ontology" ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> "CHEBI:75632" ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#inSubset> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/3_STAR> ;
                                             rdfs:label "procyanidin B2" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_75633
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_75633> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_26195> ,
                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_26267> ,
                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_50128> ,
                                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_72010> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A proanthocyanidin consisting of (−)-epicatechin and (+)-catechin units joined by a bond between positions 4 and 8' respectively  in a β-configuration.. Procyanidin B1 can be found in <em>Cinnamomum verum</em> (Ceylon cinnamon, in the rind, bark or cortex), in <em>Uncaria guianensis</em> (cat's claw, in the root), and in <em>Vitis vinifera</em> (common grape vine, in the leaf) or in peach." ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> "chebi_ontology" ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> "CHEBI:75633" ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#inSubset> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/3_STAR> ;
                                             rdfs:label "procyanidin B1" .


