###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_84403
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_84403> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17761> ;
                                             <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A phytoceramide is a ceramide where the sphingoid base is hydroxylated at position 4. These backbone bases can be 14 to 20 carbons long, either straight chain or branched. The N-linked fatty acids are typically saturated or monounsaturated with chain lengths from 14 to 26 carbon atoms; the presence of a hydroxyl group on carbon 2 is fairly common. In the illustrated generalised structure, R1 = OH, OX (where X = acyl, glycosyl, phosphate, phosphonate, etc.), or H." ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> "chebi_ontology" ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> "CHEBI:84403" ;
                                             <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#inSubset> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/3_STAR> ;
                                             rdfs:label "phytoceramides" .


